6. Events of Default: The borrowing arrangements entered into by our Company contains standard events of 
default, including but not limited to: 

a. classification of any borrowing account of our Company as a special mention account (SMA) or any 
similar category by any lender in accordance with applicable regulatory guidelines;  

b. downgrade of the credit rating of our Company by any credit rating agency beyond the levels stipulated 
under the relevant borrowing arrangements, which may result in recall of the facilities or increase in 
the applicable rate of interest; 

c. failure or delay in making payment or repayment of any principal amount, interest or other amounts 
payable under the borrowing facilities on their respective due dates; 

d. default in performance of any covenant, condition, agreement or obligation under the borrowing 
arrangements or other related transaction documents; 

e. initiation of, or reasonable apprehension of, any proceedings relating to insolvency, bankruptcy, 
liquidation, winding up, dissolution or reorganisation of our Company, or appointment of a receiver or 
liquidator in respect of all or any part of its assets, or initiation of recovery or enforcement proceedings 
against our Company; 

f. occurrence of any event which renders it unlawful for our Company or any relevant person, including 
the lenders, to perform their respective obligations under the borrowing arrangements;  

g. failure by our Company to comply with any agreements entered into with corporate counterparties in 
connection with the borrowing facilities;

