j. failure or refusal by our Company to provide documents, data or information as may be required by the 
lenders or regulatory authorities from time to time; 

k. cessation or intended cessation of business, destruction or damage of material assets, or any change in 
the general nature or scope of business, operations, management or ownership of our Company which 
could have a material adverse effect; 

l. action taken or threatened by any governmental or regulatory authority, including revocation, 
suspension or non- renewal of licences or authorisations , or imposition of conditions affecting the 
conduct of business of our Company, which could have a material adverse effect;  

m. occurrence of an event of default under any other indebtedness of our Company or recall of financial 
assistance by any other lender; 

n. occurrence of any event, condition or circumstance, including change in law, which in the opinion of 
the lender could have a material adverse effect on the business or financial condition of our Company; 

o. failure by our Company to notify the lenders of the occurrence of any default or event which is likely 
to constitute an event of default under the borrowing arrangements; 

p. enforcement or invocation of security created in relation to the borrowing facilities, including creation 
of any security interest in favour of third parties in violation of the borrowing documents; and  

q. occurrence of any other events as may be specified under the borrowing arrangements, pursuant to 
which the lenders may exercise their contractual rights, including recall, suspension or termination of 
the facilities. 

The above is an indicative list and there may be additional events of default under the various borrowing 
arrangements entered into by our Company. 

7. Consequences of Events of Default:  In terms of the facility agreements and sanction letters, in case of 
occurrence of events of default set out above, our lenders may, among others:  

a. recall of the loan and declaration of all outstanding amounts as immediately due and payable;  

b. invocation and appropriation of amounts, securities or other rights available under the borrowing 
arrangements; 

c. disclosure of the Company’s name and particulars on the website of the Credit Guarantee Fund Trust 
for Micro and Small Enterprises (CGTMSE), where applicable; 

d. classification of the loan account as overdue, special mention account (SMA) or non -performing asset 
(NPA) in accordance with applicable Reserve Bank of India guidelines; 

e. revocation or cancellation of the sanction or borrowing facilities in the event of material adverse 
changes in the financial performance of the Company or suppression, misstatement or inaccuracy of 
material information; 

f. enforcement of security and appointment of a receiver, in accordance with the facility documents and 
applicable law; 

g. appropriation or set-off of balances lying in any account of the Company maintained with the lenders 
towards outstanding dues without prior intimation;

